<title>UK: UKAV fund takes over John Mansfield.</title>
<headline>UKAV fund takes over John Mansfield.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>British timber products maker John Mansfield Group Plc said on Tuesday it had placed 166.6 million new ordinary shares at 3.0p/share with UKAV Continuation Fund.</p>
<p>The placing means UKAV owns 65.37 percent of John Mansfield. Executives advising UKAV will join the Mansfield board.</p>
<p>The company said the placing needed approval from shareholders and it would convene an extraordinary general meeting.</p>
<p>John Mansfield said the new management intended to make one or several substantial acquisitions and retain the existing business.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
